  "locales": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Question words",
      "summary": "Question words ask for information and come first.",
      "status": "draft",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "What it is",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "Question words ask for information: who, what, where, when, why, how, which and whose."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Where** do you live?",
                "**Why** is she late?",
                "**How** much is it?"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "How it works in English",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "The question word comes first, then the auxiliary and the subject. How can be joined with much, many, long and old."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "html": "<table><thead><tr><th>Word</th><th>Asks about</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>who</strong></td><td>a person</td><td><strong>Who is that?</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>where</strong></td><td>a place</td><td><strong>Where is the bank?</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>when</strong></td><td>a time</td><td><strong>When does it start?</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>how many</strong></td><td>a number</td><td><strong>How many are there?</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
